<%# The bar on the door pages -- sign in, forgot password, register -- where no
    one is signed in yet: the brand, and the theme toggle. The same bar as
    _top_menu so navbar.css paints the same ink; the brand leads back to the
    sign-in page rather than /me. The theme controller rides the nav here as it
    does on the full bar, and its connect() is what sets the theme on <html>
    from the saved preference or the system. %>
<nav class="navbar bg-chrome/80" data-controller="theme">
  <div class="navbar-start">
    <%= link_to "Clubhouse", root_path, class: "btn btn-ghost text-xl no-decoration" %>
  </div>
  <div class="navbar-end">
    <%= render "application/theme_toggle" %>
  </div>
</nav>
